            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Oil-based deck stains carry pigment in natural drying oils — typically linseed oil, tung oil, or an alkyd resin derived from modified oils — dissolved in petroleum solvents rather than water. Those oils penetrate into the wood's cell structure and cure through oxidation (reacting slowly with air) rather than by water evaporating out of an acrylic emulsion. The practical result is deeper penetration into the wood fiber, a finish that fades gradually rather than peeling, and cleanup with mineral spirits instead of soap and water.",
