            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Traditional high-VOC oil-based deck stains are restricted, not universally banned, in California under South Coast Air Quality Management District and California Air Resources Board architectural coatings rules that cap the volatile organic compound content of wood finishes. Several other states that follow similar Ozone Transport Commission-aligned VOC limits impose comparable restrictions. In practice this means some traditional oil formulas are reformulated to a compliant, lower-VOC version, sold only through specific channels, or unavailable in certain states entirely — always check the product label or manufacturer's site for your state before ordering.",
          },
        },
