            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Clean brushes, rollers, and sprayer parts with mineral spirits (paint thinner), working the solvent through the bristles until it runs clear, then wash with soap and water. The critical safety step is rag disposal: oil-soaked rags generate heat as the oil oxidizes and can spontaneously combust if balled up in a pile or trash can. Lay used rags flat outdoors to dry completely before disposal, or submerge them in a sealed metal container filled with water, and never leave a heap of oily rags indoors overnight.",
