          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Mineral-Spirit Cleanup</h3>
          <p>
            Oil-based stains don't clean up with soap and water. Brushes, roller covers, and sprayer components need to be worked through with mineral spirits (paint thinner) until the solvent runs clear, then given a final soap-and-water wash to remove residual thinner. Natural-bristle brushes hold up to mineral spirits far better than synthetic ones, which is worth knowing if you're buying application tools specifically for an oil-based job.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-6">
