            <ul class="space-y-2 text-red-900 text-sm">
              <li>• Oil-soaked rags generate heat as the oil oxidizes and can spontaneously combust if piled up</li>
              <li>• Never leave a heap of oily rags balled up in a trash can, garage corner, or laundry hamper</li>
              <li>• Lay used rags flat outdoors, spread apart, until fully dry and hardened before disposal</li>
              <li>• Alternatively, submerge rags in a sealed metal container filled with water</li>
              <li>• This applies to rags, brushes, and any applicator pads used with linseed, tung, or alkyd-based products</li>
            </ul>
